---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE, SITE_DESCRIPTION } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			import React, { useState } from 'react';
import { Target, Users, Settings, Play, CheckCircle2 } from 'lucide-react';

export default function App() {
  const [name, setName] = useState('');
  const [audience, setAudience] = useState('Students');
  const [goal, setGoal] = useState('');
  const [showResult, setShowResult] = useState(false);

  const handleAnalyze = () => {
    if (name && goal) setShowResult(true);
  };

  return (
    <div className="min-h-screen bg-slate-100 p-6 font-sans text-slate-800">
      <div className="max-w-2xl mx-auto bg-white rounded-xl shadow-lg p-8">
        <h1 className="text-3xl font-bold mb-4 flex items-center gap-3">
          <Target className="text-blue-600" /> Project Profile Consultant
        </h1>
        
        <div className="mb-8 text-slate-600 space-y-2">
          <p>Welcome to your dynamic strategy hub.</p>
          <p>Because every grand idea needs a solid structure.</p>
          <p>Therefore, I am here to help you.</p>
          <p>While you dream big, I organize details.</p>
          <p>Rather, think of me as your architect.</p>
        </div>

        {!showResult ? (
          <div className="space-y-6">
            <section className="bg-slate-50 p-6 rounded-lg border border-slate-200">
              <h2 className="text-xl font-semibold mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
                <Settings className="w-5 h-5 text-indigo-500" /> Step 1: The Core Identity
              </h2>
              <p className="mb-4 text-sm text-slate-600">
                A project needs a very clear name. Because a title sets the immediate tone. Therefore, type your new project name below.
              </p>
              <input
                type="text"
                className="w-full p-3 border rounded-md focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-400 outline-none"
                placeholder="Enter project name..."
                value={name}
                onChange={(e) => setName(e.target.value)}
              />
            </section>

            <section className="bg-slate-50 p-6 rounded-lg border border-slate-200">
              <h2 className="text-xl font-semibold mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
                <Users className="w-5 h-5 text-indigo-500" /> Step 2: The Global Audience
              </h2>
              <p className="mb-4 text-sm text-slate-600">
                Every tool must serve diverse human perspectives. Because a village elder differs from a hacker. Therefore, select your main target audience now.
              </p>
              <select
                className="w-full p-3 border rounded-md focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-400 outline-none"
                value={audience}
                onChange={(e) => setAudience(e.target.value)}
              >
                <option>Students</option>
                <option>Professionals</option>
                <option>Elders</option>
                <option>Global Public</option>
              </select>
            </section>

            <section className="bg-slate-50 p-6 rounded-lg border border-slate-200">
              <h2 className="text-xl font-semibold mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
                <Target className="w-5 h-5 text-indigo-500" /> Step 3: The Main Goal
              </h2>
              <p className="mb-4 text-sm text-slate-600">
                A journey requires a highly specific destination. Because wandering blindly wastes your precious energy. Therefore, define your primary objective right here.
              </p>
              <input
                type="text"
                className="w-full p-3 border rounded-md focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-400 outline-none"
                placeholder="e.g., Save time, connect people..."
                value={goal}
                onChange={(e) => setGoal(e.target.value)}
              />
            </section>

            <button
              onClick={handleAnalyze}
              className="w-full bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 text-white font-bold py-3 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors flex justify-center items-center gap-2"
            >
              <Play className="w-5 h-5" /> Generate Project Profile
            </button>
          </div>
        ) : (
          <div className="bg-green-50 p-6 rounded-lg border border-green-200 animate-in fade-in slide-in-from-bottom-4 duration-500">
            <h2 className="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-green-800 flex items-center gap-2">
              <CheckCircle2 className="w-6 h-6" /> Your Custom Blueprint
            </h2>
            <div className="space-y-3 text-green-900">
              <p>Here is your tailored project strategy plan.</p>
              <p>Because you provided excellent details for me.</p>
              <p>Therefore, follow this highly specific early advice.</p>
              <p>While the path is long, start right here.</p>
              
              <hr className="border-green-300 my-4" />
              
              <ul className="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 font-medium">
                <li>Your vision for "{name}" is now clearly defined.</li>
                <li>Because your audience is {audience}, listen to them closely.</li>
                <li>Therefore, adapt your new features accordingly.</li>
                <li>While pursuing "{goal}", stay very flexible always.</li>
                <li>Rather, treat any early failures as valuable lessons.</li>
              </ul>
              
              <button
                onClick={() => setShowResult(false)}
                className="mt-6 bg-green-600 hover:bg-green-700 text-white font-bold py-2 px-4 rounded transition-colors"
              >
                Start Over
              </button>
            </div>
          </div>
        )}
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
